{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically queried the workspace multiple times, identified both preoperative and postoperative phases through dialogue, built a complete medication/allergy checklist, explicitly avoided unsafe medication directives (never treating cefazolin as home medication, never telling family to self-manage anticoagulants), provided specific red-flag symptoms, and obtained teach-back. No serious responsibility-chain error is present. Two high-order points (HO1 hidden-source discovery of non-prescription items, HO2 correction of family's misconceptions about 'anti-inflammatory' vs. 'preoperative anti-infective') were triggered and completed with meaningful trajectory impact. This meets Strong (Grade 4) but not Perfect because only two HOs were completed and one minor non-chain defect (incomplete final teach-back on pre-admission medication timing) prevents Grade 5.",
